# Spark identity

One job under `spark/identity_resolution/`. No Spark Streaming and no Spark SQL marts (ADR-006). Flink owns streams; dbt owns Gold.

## What it writes

- `graph_logic.py` is the rules source. `identity_resolution_job.py` mirrors it in DataFrames.
- `event_contract.py` and `canonical_events.py` promote Bronze `*_records` to `silver.*_events`, `*_quarantine`, and `*_duplicates`. The job fails if input rows do not equal those three counts.
- Only a verified v1.3 account-to-loyalty login merges (ADR-003). Devices are never graph nodes.
- Iceberg `silver.identity_resolution`, `silver.identity_edges`, `silver.loyalty_link_claims` and `silver.device_session_associations`, plus `consumer_current/*` exports. Spectrum reads the manifest, never an Iceberg `data/` dir.

## Commands

```powershell
.\scripts\local\run_local_stack.ps1 -Task spark
.\.venv\Scripts\python.exe spark\identity_resolution\generate_fixture.py --check
.\.venv\Scripts\python.exe tests\integration\verify_spark_identity.py
```

Local submit is Docker Compose profile `spark` (`infra/docker/spark`), not a host Spark install. Cloud submit (`deploy_platform.ps1` or the marketing DAG) is `spark-submit --py-files graph_logic.py,canonical_events.py,consumer_exports.py,event_contract.py identity_resolution_job.py`.

## Traps

- Do not hand-edit `transformation/dbt_project/seeds/silver/identity_resolution.csv` or `device_session_associations.csv`. Regenerate them with `generate_fixture.py`. CI runs `--check`.
- Tests import the package; spark-submit imports the scripts. Keep the `try/except` import.
- GraphFrames checkpoints go to gitignored `.local/graphframes-checkpoints`.
- Pins: Spark 3.4.1 (EMR 6.15 parity), Iceberg runtime 1.4.3, GraphFrames 0.8.3-spark3.4-s_2.12.
